# Copy to .env before the first `docker compose up`. The real .env is never
# committed (it is gitignored) and never baked into an image.
#
# Compose reads this file for ${...} interpolation, the FreeLLMAPI proxy gets
# ENCRYPTION_KEY from it, and the rag container mounts it at /app/.env so the
# console's Settings tab can write provider keys back. Provider keys belong here
# as NAME=value (matching an `api_key_env` in config.docker.yaml) or in the
# FreeLLMAPI dashboard on :3001.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. Your home folder on the machine running Docker.
#   macOS: /Users/yourname      Linux: /home/yourname
# docker-compose bind-mounts it at this SAME absolute path inside the
# container. That is what makes the console's folder browser and vault
# switcher show real paths instead of an invented mount point -- and it means
# every vault under your home folder works without editing docker-compose.yml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RAG_HOST_HOME=/Users/yourname

# WINDOWS ONLY. A Linux container cannot mount onto a drive-letter path, so name
# where your home folder should appear inside it. start.ps1 sets both lines for
# you; by hand it is, for C:\Users\you:
#   RAG_HOST_HOME=C:/Users/you
#   RAG_CONTAINER_HOME=/c/Users/you
# Leave it commented out on macOS and Linux: the two sides are then the same path.
# RAG_CONTAINER_HOME=

# FreeLLMAPI needs a 32-byte hex key (it encrypts the provider keys you add via
# its dashboard). Make one:
#   Windows: powershell -c "[Convert]::ToHexString((1..32|%{Get-Random -Max 256}))"
#   Mac/Lin: openssl rand -hex 32
#
# ONCE SET, KEEP IT. The keys you add in the :3001 dashboard are encrypted with
# this value and stored in the `freellmapi-data` docker volume, which outlives
# this file. Change the key and every stored key reads as "[decrypt failed]" --
# recover by restoring the old value, or reset the store:
#   docker compose down && docker volume rm <project>_freellmapi-data
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# From a repo checkout only: name the compose project, so the volumes are called
# noetrix_* rather than after the folder (deploy/docker -> docker_*). Leave this
# UNSET in an unpacked release archive, whose existing volumes are named after
# the archive's folder.
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=noetrix

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host ports, if the default ones are taken (all bound to 127.0.0.1). The two
# RAG ports are also the numbers the servers listen on inside the container, so
# the console finds the query API at the remapped port.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOETRIX_API_PORT=8051
# NOETRIX_CONSOLE_PORT=8052
# NOETRIX_PROXY_PORT=3001

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional provider keys, one per backend in the `providers:` registry. Leave
# them unset to generate through the FreeLLMAPI proxy instead. The console's
# Settings tab shows WHICH of these are set (never their values) and can write
# them here for you. Nothing is billed until you select that backend.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# FREELLMAPI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=

# MiniMax M3 Token Plan. Use the Subscription Key from Billing > Token Plan
# (sk-cp-...). A pay-as-you-go sk-api- key is a different credential and does
# not consume the plan quota.
MINIMAX_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face token, for gated models (EmbeddingGemma 2) and higher rate limits.
# HF_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional services (they only start when you ask for their compose profile).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PaddleOCR language for scanned pages: en, ch, fr, german, korean, japan, ru,
# es, pt, it, ar, hi, latin, cyrillic, devanagari, ...
# PADDLE_OCR_LANG=en

# External reranker (--profile rerank). Put a reranker GGUF in RERANK_MODEL_DIR
# and name it here; llama.cpp serves it at :8102 with /v1/rerank.
# RERANK_MODEL_DIR=./models
# RERANK_MODEL_FILE=bge-reranker-v2-m3-Q4_K_M.gguf
# RERANK_CTX=8192

# GPU services (docker-compose.gpu.yml, NVIDIA only): which physical card.
# NOETRIX_GPU_INDEX=0
